%%center June 2025 
%%textfont Times-Roman 14


%%begintext align
This is a (partial) collection of the tunes from the Monaro Folk Society's Settlers Sessions tune book. The tunes listed here are ones available from the archive. Others are included in the full collection, available elsewhere.

Most of these tunes were collected from Australia's traditional players. A few contemporary tunes are included because the folk process still exists and there are some good ones. (Please observe copyright where appropriate.)

Some tunes stand alone; others fit together as sets and some of these sets make good dance sets. Use your judgement. Treat the script provided as a guide. There are no 'correct' chords, any ornamentation is optional and the notes played sometimes owe more to the instrument, the musician and the moment than they do to what is written down. Be adventurous and feel free to 'folk' the script, traditional players certainly did.

Enjoy the music.

My thanks to the composers whose tunes are included. I have contacted those I could and I hope that those I have been unable to contact are happy to have their music played and valued.

%%endtext

