X:1
T:Watching the Cattle
T:Lawrie Cobley's Cattle Lullaby
% NFF Book 2007
S:collected from Lawrie Cobley, Bawden's Bridge, NSW
S:collected by Dave de Hugard
Z:transcribed by Dave de Hugard
H:Lawrie Cobley was a Aboriginal cattle drover in Queensland. He played this 
H:tune on his harmonica to let the mob know where he was at night. It has an unusual 
H:repetitive and hypnotic melody, a lullaby that cycles endlessly.
N:Lawrie Cobley was a fiddler & accordionist who lived at Bawden's Bridge
N:via Grafton NSW. He was recorded 1996/97.
O:Australia, NSW, Bawden's Bridge
R:Air
F:Watching_the_Cattle.mp3 Watching the Cattle - played by Greg O'Leary
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:A
