T:Rita Baker's Polka
% NFF Book 2006
S:collected from Rita Baker, Gulgong, NSW
S:John Meredith Collection, NLA, Bib ID 677305
Z:converted to abc by John Furlonger
B:J Meredith, R Covell, & P Brown, Folk Songs of Australia Vol 2, UNSW Press, 1987, p19
N:Rita learned this tune from her father. The tune had no name.
H:This is a really easy, very effective polka, variants of which come from an area 
H:known as the as the Nulla, near Kempsey, NSW. The Nulla has been a hotbed for 
H:fiddlers over the past 100 years. It is where David Gordon Kirkpatrick, 
H:aka Slim Dusty, came from. - Greg O'Leary
%O:Australia, NSW, Gulgong
